{ Does White have time to capture the g4-pawn ? } 1. Nxg4
{ White can afford to take the pawn. In fact, this is the fastest and safest route to secure a draw. }
1... Bxg4 2. Kxg4 Kb5 3. Kf4 Kxa5 4. Ke3
{ Draw. The king reaches the key c1-square. White's last move seems so obvious, but the databases reveal that white players have erred in this position, e.g.   50.Ke4 ?  Kb4  51.Kd3  Kb3  52.Kd2  Kb2  0-1, Berger-Mason, Breslau 1889. At the time of this game, endgame theory was of course still in its infancy.   See Ending 5. }
