{ White just exchanged Queens on f2. Make him regret that decision! } 1. Qxf2+
{ White must keep the queens on and suffer a little while longer in a drawn endgame. The simplest way to do this is by playing   58.Qa1+ = }
1... Kxf2 2. Ke4
{ This forces Black to find the only accurate move in this position. } 2... Kg3
{ 59...h5 ??  60.Kf4 !  and White will capture the pawn. } 3. Ke3
{ 60.Kf5  h5  and the pawn will promote. } 3... h5 4. Ke2 Kg2
{ When the kings face one another like this, the pawn always promotes, even if it were still on its second rank. }
