{ Can White win the game ? } 1. Rf7
{ White wins by giving up the pawn to imprison the king in the wrong corner. White needs the rook on f7 so that the king can't escape via f8:   76.g8=Q+ ?  Kxg8  77.Kg6  Kf8 !  and the king escapes. }
1... Be5 2. g8=Q+ Kxg8 3. Kg6 Bg3
{ The bishop tries to stay safe in the shadow of the White king, but there are not enough squares to hide. }
4. Rf3 Bd6 5. Rd3 Be7 6. Rc3
{ The fastest way.   81.Rb3  Bd6  82.Rb6  Bg3  83.Rf6  Bh4  84.Rf4  Another example is   84.Rf3  (actually move 83 in the game)  Bd8  85.Rd3  Bh4  86.Rd4  1-0, Wojtyra-Cetwinski  (place + date unknown)  .  84...Bg3  85.Rg4  Bd6  86.Rd4  Be7  87.Ra4  1-0. There is no way to avoid the loss of the bishop. }
6... Bf8 7. Rc8 Kh8 8. Rxf8# { See Ending 6. } *

