{ Can White win the game ? } 1. Ke6
{ By means of a pawn sacrifice, White finds a way to exploit the weaknesses in Black's camp. }
1... Nxf4+
{ 53...Kf8  also fails:  54.Rf7+  Ke8   54...Kg8  55.Ke7  Kh8  56.Kf8  55.Rf6 !  Nxf6  56.Kxf6  and the king will capture the pawn, maintaining control over the key squares. }
2. Kf6 Ng2
{ Once more we see that a knight separated from the king is bound to be lost. Another variation is   54...Kh8  55.Rd4  g5  56.Rd7  g4   56...Nh5+  57.Kxg5  Ng7  58.Kg6  Ne6  59.Rd6  Nf4+  60.Kf5  57.Rd4  +- }
3. Kxg6 Nf4+ 4. Kg5 Ne6+ 5. Kf6 Nf8 6. Rd8 { 1-0.  See Ending 3 & Ending 8. } *

