{ How should Black capture the pawn ? } 1... Kxd7
{ The way to prevent White from reaching the key squares is by capturing with the king.  Capturing with the rook loses:   77...Rxd7 ?  78.Rd3+  Ke6  79.Rxd7  Kxd7  80.Kg3 !  Ke6  81.Kg4  Kf6  82.Kf4  and White conquers the key squares. }
2. Ra7+ Ke8 3. Rxe7+ Kxe7 4. Kg3 { 80.Ke3  Kf7 !  leads to the same. } 4... Kf7
{ An accurate move, preventing White from reaching the key squares.   80...Kf6 ?  81.Kf4  Ke6  82.Kg5  Kf7  83.Kf5  Kg7  84.Ke6  Kf8  85.f4  Ke8  86.f5  Kf8  87.Kf6  Kg8  88.Ke7  +-   80...Ke6 ?  81.Kg4  Kf6  82.Kf4  +- }
5. Kg4 Kg6 6. Kf4 Kf6 { Draw.  See Ending 3. } *

