{ Does Black have time to capture the pawn and escape from the wrong corner ? }
1... Bxa6
{ Black can afford to capture the pawn, provided he finds the right move on the next turn. }
2. Ka5 { Now, there is only one move to save the game. The right move is } 2...
Bd3
{ 90...Bc4 ?  Wrong !  91.Rc6  Bb3  92.Rc7+  Kb8  93.Kb6  Ba2  94.Rc2  Be6  95.Re2  Bd7  96.Rh2  1-0.  Also losing is   90...Be2 ?  on account of  91.Rf7+  Kb8  92.Kb6  Kc8  93.Kc6  Kd8  94.Kd6  Kc8  95.Rc7+  Kd8   95...Kb8  96.Kc6  and the king is confined.  96.Rc2 !  (The bishop doesn't have a single good square.)  Bd3  97.Rd2  And the bishop is lost. }
3. Rf7+ { 91.Rd6  Be2 } 3... Kb8 4. Kb6 Kc8 5. Kc6 Be4+
{ This check makes the difference. } 6. Kd6 Bg2 7. Rc7+ Kb8
{ And with the bishop on the long diagonal, the side with the rook cannot complete the plan to confine the Black king in the wrong corner.  See Ending 6 & Ending 7. }
