{ Choose between 38. h5 and 38. Kf4. } 1. Kf4
{ The White king should oscillate between f3 and f4. Black, on the other hand, must play ...g6-g5 to capture the e4-pawn.  Exchanging with   38.h5 ?  is premature. White's king can't reach the critical c1/c2-squares in time to imprison Black's:  gxh5+  39.Kxh5  Kxe4  40.Kxh6  Kd3  41.Kg5  Kc3  42.Kf4  Kb2  43.Ke3  Kxa2  44.Kd2  Kb2  -+  White is too slow. }
1... a6 2. Kf3 Ke5 3. Ke3 g5 4. hxg5 hxg5
{ The distant passer, while a nuisance, can't pose enough problems to keep White's king away from the critical c1-/c2-squares. }
5. Kf3 Kd4
{ 42...a5  43.Kg4  amounts to the same:  Kxe4  44.Kxg5  Kd3  45.Kf4  Kc2  46.Ke3  Kb2  47.Kd2  Kxa2  48.Kc2 =  Imprisoning the Black king. }
6. Kg4 Kxe4 7. Kxg5 Kd3 8. Kf4 Kc2 9. Ke3 Kb2 10. Kd2 Kxa2 11. Kc2 Ka1
{ Draw.  See Ending 5. } *

