{ Is 54... Ne4 winning ? } 1... Ne4
{ 54... Ne4 is winning, but Black has to know what to do on his next move. In the game, Black erred: }
2. Bxe4 g4+
{ would have led to an easy win.   55...e2 ?  A mistake.  56.Kf2 !  Clearly, Grischuk had missed this.   56.Kxe2 ?  Kxe4  57.Kf2  Kf4  58.Kg2  Kg4  and Black would control the key squares.  56...Kxe4  57.Kxe2 !  White keeps the opposition, denying Black's king control over the key squares.  Kf4  58.Kf2  g4  59.Kg2  g3  60.Kg1  Kf3  61.Kf1  g2+  62.Kg1  Kg3  Draw.   See Ending 2. }
