{ According to my database, White players have chosen the following moves in this position: 77. Ke5, 77. Kg6 and 77. Kf6. Which ones are correct ? There are two winning moves. }
1. Kg6
{ This is the most natural winning move, for instance:   77.Kf6 ??  It's hard to believe that such a strong player would ever make such a dreadful move.  Kf8  78.e7+  Ke8  79.Ke6  Draw.   77.Ke5 !  is the other winning move: 1-0 Tomczak-Graf, Poznan 2007. }
1... Kf8 2. Kf6
{ and we've reached the basic winning position with the pawn on the sixth rank: 1-0 Hatzis-Bakratsas-Fidrilakis, Greece tt 2017.  See Ending 2. }
