{ Is the knight able to prevent the pawn from queening ? } 1... g3 2. Ng5
{ The only square for the knight  (barring direct attacks on the pawn)  , enabling White to save the game, regardless of who is to move. }
2... Kg1
{ 54...g2  55.Nf3+ !   55.Kb5  Kg3 !  -+  55...Kg3  56.Ng1  The knight is in front of the pawn, thus ensuring a draw. }
