{ Choose between 66. Nb4+ and 66. Nc1+. } 1. Nb4+
{ Getting the knight onto the right circuit is by itself no guarantee for a draw. Depending on the position of the enemy king, you have to choose the right square.   66.Nc1+ ??  In this case, the other option was called for.  Kb1 !  Now, the knight has a limited choice lest the pawn queen on its own.  67.Ne2   67.Nb3  Kb2  -+  The knight is powerless to stop the pawn.  67...Kb2 !  0-1. }
1... Kb3 2. Kc5
{ Once the king lends a helping hand, things become so much easier.  Notwithstanding   67.Nd3  is also good enough.   See Ending 12. }
