{ Can the knight get onto the right circuit ? } 1. Kf6
{ With correct play, White can keep the knight at bay. The position visually contrasts with the previous diagram, where the knight was in time even though it was further away. Fending off the knight on a three-square diagonal is optimal technique: the knight would have to spend three moves to give a single check. }
1... Nc2
{ 70...Ne2  71.h5  Ng3  72.h6  And the pawn will promote.   70...Nf3  71.h5  Nh2  72.Kf5 !  +- }
2. h5 Ne3 3. Kg5 { Again, optimally fending off the cavalier. } 3... Nc4
{ Beliavsky resigned in view of } 4. h6 Ne5 5. h7 Nf7+ 6. Kf6 Nh8 7. Kg7
{ See Ending 12. } *

[Event "?"]
[Site "?"]
