{ Choose between 56. h6 and 56. e7+. } 1. e7+
{ 56.h6 ?  h5-h6 is the move of a player who doesn't know what it feels like to get checkmated in one of the corners of the chessboard by a lone knight.  Nd3 !  Black is alert and moves the knight closer.  57.e7+  Ke8  58.Kg7  Kxe7  59.Kxh7 ?!  The king is five moves away from certain death. White could have put up slightly more stubborn resistance by keeping the king next to the black pawn without capturing it. However, against correct play this also loses:   59.Kg8  Nf4  60.Kg7  Ne6+  61.Kg8  Kf6  62.Kh8  Kf7 !  and White must face the music:  63.Kxh7  Ng5+  64.Kh8  Kf8  65.h7  Nf7#  59...Kf7 !  60.Kh8  Nf4  61.Kh7  Ne6  62.Kh8  Nf8 !  0-1. It is checkmate in one move. }
1... Ke8 2. Kg7 Kxe7 3. Kxh7 Kf7 4. Kh6
{ leads to a clear draw.  See Ending 12 & Ending 14. } *

