{ Does Black win by exchanging rooks ? } 1... Rxg5
{ Black wins, since the White pawn will only reach the seventh rank. In fact, this is the only way to win the game. }
2. hxg5 { 74.Kxg5  Kg3  75.Kxg6  Kxh4  76.Kf5  Kg3  -+  . } 2... h4 3. Kxg6 h3
4. Kf7 h2 5. g6 h1=Q 6. g7 Qh7
{ Black won twelve moves later by means of a well-known procedure: move the queen closer and closer with check until the enemy king is forced to step in front of its pawn, thus gaining the necessary tempi for the king to approach, step by step. }
7. Kf8 Qf5+ 8. Ke7 Qg6 9. Kf8 Qf6+ 10. Kg8 Kg3 11. Kh7 Qf7 12. Kh8 Qh5+ 13. Kg8
Kg4 14. Kf8 Qf5+ 15. Ke7 Qg6 16. Kf8 Qf6+ 17. Kg8 Kg5 18. Kh7
{ 0-1.  See Ending 16. } *

