{ Only one move wins. Which one ? } 1. Qb7+
{ Perhaps White couldn't find another check after   59.Qe2+ ?  White should be careful not to give just any random queen check. This move prepares a trick which actually won White the game, but objectively, allowing the Black pawn another step forward is the wrong idea since the king is outside the winning zone; now the position is a theoretical draw.  c2  60.Kd4  This tricky position has claimed many victims. My database reveals thirteen games with identical or symmetrical positions. Seven timed did the side with the pawn err.  Kb1 ??   60...Ka1 =  is the right move, as you can find out for yourself.  61.Kc3  c1=Q+  62.Kb3  1-0. }
1... Kc1
{ But after   59...Ka1  allows the queen to come closer by means of checks:  60.Qa6+  Kb2  61.Qb5+  Ka2  62.Qa4+  Kb2  63.Qb4+  +- }
2. Kd4 { the king has time to enter the winning zone: } 2... c2 3. Kd3 Kd1 4.
Qh1# { See Ending 19. } *

