{ Can Black win the game ? } 1... Qh7
{ The winning move.   69...Ke5 ?  Allows the White king into the corner, while Black lacks the tempi needed to bring his own king closer. Black wins as long as he doesn't let the enemy king escape via the right side of the pawn. In the game he achieved this only because of his opponent's inexpert play.  70.Ke7 ?  But the king comes out via the wrong side of the pawn, a phenomenal blunder !   70.Kg7 !  holds the draw for the reason stated above: the Black king has no time to come closer. In fact, it can neither reach e7 nor g6 in a single move:  Qg4+  71.Kh7  Qh5+  72.Kg7  Qg5+  73.Kh7  Qf6  74.Kg8  Qg6+  75.Kh8 =  70...Qb7+  71.Ke8  Ke6  0-1. }
2. Ke8 Ke5 3. f8=Q Ke6
{ and checkmate is inevitable.  See Ending 18 & Ending 19. } *

