{ White can choose between 58. Rd7, 58. e8=Q and 58. Rc8. Do any of these moves win ? }
1. Rc8
{ The rook should be employed to win the c4-pawn, when the win would be a piece of cake.   58.Rd7 ?  There is one winning move, but it's not the most obvious one, played in the game. You'll see here an exceptional case of a queen unable to beat a pawn on the sixth rank.  Bxd7+  59.Kxd7  Kd2  60.e8=Q  c3  Extraordinary ! The white queen has no checks.  61.Qe5  c2  62.Qb2  Kd1  63.Qd4+  Ke2  64.Qc3  Kd1  65.Qd3+  Kc1  66.Kc6  Kb2  67.Qd2  Kb1  68.Qb4+  Ka2  69.Qc3  Kb1  70.Qb3+  Ka1  Draw.  Or   58.e8=Q ?  Bxe8  59.Rxe8  Kd4  60.Rd8+  Ke4  61.Rc8  Kd4  62.Kf5  c3  63.Kf4  Kd3  64.Kf3  c2 = }
