{ Can White win the game ? } 1. Kh3
{ White can win the game, but he has to voluntarily move the king to the h-file, allowing it to be cut off, to exploit the power of the pawn duo. Kh3 is easily winning because of the unstoppable pawn duo:   52.Kf5 ??  This move leads to a drawn queen vs. pawn-on-the-seventh endgame.  Rf1+  53.Ke6  Rxf7 !  54.Kxf7  e4  55.g6  Kf2 !  Getting the king's position right. Here the newly born queen won't be able to give any checks.  56.g7  e3  57.g8=Q  e2  Mista must have felt extremely frustrated here. How often do you get the chance to play queen vs. central pawn on the seventh, and when it finally happens, it turns out to be an exception !  58.Qe8  e1=Q  59.Qxe1+  Kxe1  Draw. }
1... Rf1 2. g6 { followed by g6-g7.  See Ending 16. } *

