{ What is the best way for Black to sacrifice his rook ? } 1... Rf8
{ had to be played: in this variation, the king on a6 is fast enough.   72...Rf7 ??  Pinning the pawn to sacrifice the rook on c7 loses. It makes a huge difference whether the White king is on a7 or on a6.  73.Kxa6  Rxc7  74.Rxc7  Kf3  75.Rf7+  Gaining a tempo !  Ke4  76.Rg7  Kf4  From a6, the king reaches the critical square in three moves.  77.Kb5  g4  78.Kc4  g3  79.Kd3  Kf3  Once again, a version of the standard diagram A position, with White to play.  80.Rf7+  Kg2  81.Ke2  Kg1  82.Rg7  g2  83.Rg8  Kh2  84.Kf2  Kh1  85.Rh8# }
2. c8=Q+ Rxc8 3. Rxc8 Kf3 4. Rf8+ { Our classic tempo-gaining scheme. } 4...
Ke3 5. Rg8 Kf4
{ and now it turns out that the king is four steps away from the critical d3-square: }
6. Kb6
{ No matter how hard White tries, the king won't get there in three moves: }
6... g4 7. Kc5 g3 8. Kd4 Kf3 9. Kd3 { See Ending 28. } *

