{ What is the best way for Black to sacrifice the rook ? } 1... Rh7
{ Here, it's necessary to pin the pawn to sacrifice the rook on the e7-square, as tactics prevent Black from making some other useful move. Other moves lose, including the logical retreat with the king. Let's see the variations:   50...Ka3 ?  51.Rc3+ !!  (a devilish intermediate check, making the Black king lose a vital tempo)  Ka4   51...Ka2  52.Rc8  Rh7  53.Rb8  +-  52.Rc8  Rh7  53.Kd6  Rxe7  54.Kxe7  b4  55.Kd6  b3  56.Kc5  Ka3  57.Kc4  +-  Waiting with   50...Rg8  is not an option, as White simply improves his position:  51.Rc8  +- }
2. Re1
{ Lets Black improve his king.   51.Rc8  seems a bit more logical:  Ka3 !  52.Kd6  Rxe7 !  53.Kxe7  b4  54.Kd6  b3  55.Kc5  b2 =   51.Kd8  Rxe7  52.Kxe7  Ka3  and now a check from the front is not so effective:  53.Ra1+  Kb2 ! =  The king is unimpressed by the enemy rook. }
2... Kc3 3. Kc6 Rxe7 4. Rxe7 b4 5. Kb5 { Going round is too slow. } 5... b3 6.
Re3+ Kc2 7. Re2+ Kc3 8. Ka4 b2 9. Re1 Kc2 10. Ka3 b1=Q 11. Rxb1 Kxb1
{ Draw.  See Ending 23. } *

