{ 55.b5 ?  Shoving the pawn forward while preventing the '...Rf5-trick', but despite these virtues, this is a losing move.  axb5+  56.Kxb5  The problem is that the pawn can't be captured, so now the king remains on the wrong side.   56.cxb5  Rf4+ !  57.Ka5  Rg4  -+  56...g1=Q  57.Rxg1  Rxg1  When the king is on the wrong side of the pawn, all you have to do is count the tempi each player needs to either help the pawn become a queen, or prevent it from doing so.  58.c5  Kg4  59.Kc6 !?  Kf5  60.Kd6  Rd1+  61.Ke7  Rc1  62.Kd6  Kf6  63.c6  Rd1+  64.Kc7  Ke7  0-1. }
