{ Is there any difference between 78. Rxf7 and 78. Kxf7 ? } 1. Kxf7
{ There is a huge difference between 78. Kxf7 and 78. Rxf7: 78. Kxf7 forces Black into a losing knight-in-the-corner vs. rook endgame.   78.Rxf7 ?  This move fails, because the White king blocks the rook's way to the other side of the board, so White will not be able to give side checks.  h5  79.Rg7+   79.Kf6  h4 =  and White, unable to give a check on the fourth rank, can't bring his king any further: a theoretical draw.  79...Kf3  80.Rh7  Kg4  81.Kf6  h4  White can't win. Please note, however, that White would be winning if he were able to give a horizontal check.  82.Ke5  Kg3  83.Ke4  h3  84.Ke3  Kg2 !  85.Rg7+  Kf1  It's a drawn position, although according to the database White won. }
