[FEN "8/5R2/8/6p1/7p/6k1/3K4/8 w - - 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]

{ Can White win the game ? } 1. Ke2
{ White is winning because his king is active. The winning procedure involves bringing the king even closer. }
1... g4 2. Kf1
{ The White king wants to sneak in front of the pawns, so Black's next move is forced. }
2... Kh2 3. Rf2+
{ Now either Black's king must move to the back rank or else he must lose a pawn. }
3... Kh1 4. Rf4 h3 { Setting up a clever trap. } 5. Kf2
{ Not falling for   59.Rxg4 ?  h2 !  and there would be no way to avoid stalemate. }
5... h2 6. Re4 { 1-0.  See Ending 28. } *

