{ Can White successfully deal with the pawns ? } 1. Rh4
{ White can win thanks to his active king. First, however, he must find the right place for his rook.   72.Rd4 ?  Placing the rook behind the passed pawn, however natural, is not the right plan against two connected passed pawns, and throws away the win.  d2  73.Kc2  Black has not much to fear any more: the position is an easy draw.  Ke1   73...Kf2  or   73...Kf1  is also a draw.  74.Rd3  Ke2  75.Rxe3+  Kxe3  76.Kd1  Kd3  Draw. }
1... d2 2. Rh2+ { Perhaps this move was hard to find. } 2... Ke1 3. Rh1+ Ke2 4.
Kc2 { See Ending 31. } *

