{ Can Black make a draw ? } 1... Rg2
{ was the only correct move, preventing the switch in pole position, and if   77...Ke5 ??  We've seen this kind of position before, and we will keep seeing more of them. Remember the basic techniques: switch pole position, and play tag. Black can make an easy draw by watching out for a switch in pole position, but in the game the player with the Black pieces became obsessed with playing tag:  78.Kg7 !  1-0. White switches pole position, and the Black king and rook are uncoordinated. Had the king been on d6, the game would have been drawn. }
2. g7 { there follows } 2... Ke5 { playing tag.  See Ending 32. } *

