{ Is 85. Qb6+ winning ? } 1. Qb6+ { The easiest way to win. } 1... Rxb6 2. axb6
Rb4 3. Kc6
{ It's never too late to fall into Prokes's trap, as many naive and overconfident players have experienced. If   87.c6 ?  hoping to sacrifice the pawn and win with a single pawn against the rook, there follows the intermediate check  Rb5+ !  with a draw. }
3... Kg6 4. Kb7
{ Switching pole position is the only way to win: the Black king may seem miles away, but actually, it only lacks one tempo to draw the game. }
4... Kf7 5. c6 { 1-0.  See Ending 32. } *

