3... Bc3 4. Ke6
{ White threatens 60. Be5 and there is only one way to counter that threat: }
4... Bg7 5. Bc5 { 60.Be5  Kf8 ! = } 5... Bc3 6. Bb4 Bb2 7. Be7 Bc3
{ 62...Bg7 ??  63.Bd6 !  Bf8   63...Bh6  64.Kf6  Bf8  65.Bf4  +-  64.Bxf8  +- }
8. Ba3 Bd4 9. Kf5 Bc3 10. Bd6 Bb2 11. Kg5 Bg7 12. Kf4 Bc3 13. Kf5 Bb2
