{ Can White save the game ? } 1. Nf4
{ The knight is miles away, and on top of that, Black has two pawns. The a-pawn however is of no use, so Black plans its timely sacrifice. With correct defence, White can establish a well-known theoretical draw. This is the only correct route towards the d3-square.   73.Nf2 ?  fails because of  Bc2  74.Kxa2  Kf4  75.Nh3+  Ke3  76.Ka3  Bf5  77.Ng1  Be6  and White can't hold the position. }
1... c2 2. Nd3 Bc4 3. Nc1
{ White has achieved a well-known theoretical position. Black can't do anything meaningful with the a2-pawn. }
3... Ke4 4. Kb2 a1=Q+ 5. Kxa1 Ke3 6. Kb2 Kd2 7. Ka1 Kc3 8. Nb3 Bb5 9. Nc1 Ba4
10. Ka2 Be8 11. Ka1 Bf7 12. Nb3 { Draw.  See Ending 39. } *

