{ Is this endgame winning for White ? } 1. Ke6
{ This is a winning endgame: the presence of the c3-pawn, while a factor to reckon with, changes neither the assessment of the position nor the main idea.   70.Bb3 ?  This move fails as it lets the Black king out of the corner. Correct would be to advance the king first to prevent the enemy monarch from reaching the f8-square.  c2 !  A miraculous escape.  71.Bxc2  Kg8 !  72.Bb3+  Kf8 !  We've reached a theoretical draw with g- and h-pawns on the sixth.  73.Ba4  Bc3  74.Kg5  Bb2  75.Bd1  Ba1  Draw. }
1... Kg8 2. Ke7 { followed by Bb3 and Kf7, winning.  See Ending 41. } *

