2. Bxg4+ Kxg4
{ Draw. Kamsky didn't insist, as the defence is straightforward, e.g. } 3. Kd2
Kf3 4. Bd4 Bd5 5. Bc5 e3+ 6. Bxe3 c3+ 7. Kxc3 { See Ending 44. } *

