2... Ba6 3. Kc5 Kd7 4. Kb6
{ To illustrate that advancing the b-pawn prematurely can be a big mistake, have a look at the following variation:   68.b5 ?!  Bb7  69.b6 ??  Ke6  and the White king can't get through. }
4... Bc8 { 68...Bd3  69.b5  Kc8  70.Kc6  Be4+  71.Kc5  Bd3  72.b6 } 5. b5 Kd8
6. Ka7 Kd7 7. b6 Kc6 8. f5 Kd7 9. b7 Bxb7 10. Kxb7 { 1-0.  See Ending 50. } *

