[SetUp "1"]

{ Can Black win the game ? } 1... Kg5
{ Black can get a theoretically winning endgame by transforming the position into one with two extra pawns separated by four files. }
2. Bf7 h4 3. gxh4+ Bxh4
{ The creation of the first passer. Now all that is required is to bring the king to the queenside to get in ... a7-a6 and ...b6-b5. }
4. Be6 Kf4 5. Bc8 Be7 6. Bd7 Bd6 7. Kf1 Kf3 8. Bc8 g3 9. Bb7+ Ke3 10. Bc6 Kd2
11. Kg2 Kc3 12. Kf3 Kb4 13. Ke3 a6 14. Kd3 b5 15. axb5 axb5
{ Now we have two passers. } 16. Bd5 Ka3 17. Kc2 b4
{ 0-1. A typical zugzwang position; White has to allow one of the pawns through. }
