{ How should White capture the pawn ? } 1. Kxh4
{ This leads to an easy win: the two passed pawns are separated by five files.  By contrast,   44.gxh4 ?  turns the b3-bishop into a wrong bishop in view of the colour of the queening square h8: with  Kg7  Black would then achieve an easy draw by sacrificing his bishop for the a-pawn at some opportune moment. }
1... Ba5
{ 1-0. Lanka had seen enough, knowing that promoting a pawn is easy when the pawns are so far separated, for example: }
2. Kh5 Bb4 3. g4 Bd2 4. Bc2 { zugzwang } 4... Bc1 5. a5 Bd2 6. a6 Be3 7. g5+
Kg7 8. Kg4 Ba7 9. Kf5 { and the king heads for the a-pawn. } *

