{ Is the breakthrough 50... h4 winning for Black ? } 1... h4
{ ...h5-h4 leads to an endgame with a central and rook's pawn, which Black can win by force by means of the typical king march. }
2. fxg5
{ At best,   51.gxh4  leads to the same endgame since White will be forced to give up the f4-pawn later on. In addition, Black can play  d4+ !  exploiting the fact that if  52.Kxd4  gxh4  the pawn will inevitably promote. }
2... h3 3. g4+ Kxg5 4. Be5 Kxg4 5. Bh2
{ The king can't get through between the pawns, so its only viable route is via the kingside by means of the typical detour. At several points during the course of this long but effective procedure, Black must use zugzwang. }
5... Kf5 6. Kd4 Ke6 7. Kc5 Kd7 8. Bg3 Kc8 9. Bh2 Kb7 10. Bg3 Ka6 11. Bc7 Bg2
{ Zugzwang. } 12. Kb4 Bf3 13. Kc5 Be4 14. Bd6 Ka5 15. Kd4 Ka4 16. Kc3 Bg2
{ Again, zugzwang. } 17. Kc2 Bf3 18. Kc3 Be4 19. Bh2 Ka3 20. Bd6+ Ka2 21. Bh2
Kb1 22. Bf4 Bg6 23. Kd4 Bf7 24. Kc3 Be6 { Once more, zugzwang. } 25. Kd3 Kb2
26. Kd2 Kb3 27. Kd3 Bf5+ 28. Kd2 d4 29. Be5 Kc4 30. Bh2 Kd5 31. Ke2 Ke4 32. Bc7
