{ Choose between 109... Kf8 and 109... Kg8. } 1... Kg8
{ Anticipating your opponent's intentions is often crucial to finding the right ideas in your games. In this position, White intends Kf6 to end up with a knight's pawn. The only viable method of play, therefore, is the back-rank defence.  After   109...Kf8 ?  110.Kf6  Rxf4+  111.Kxg6  Black can't reach the back-rank defence. Hence, he would end up on the losing side of a Lucena. }
