{ Is there a way Black can win the game by force ? } 1... Ra4
{ Such a logical, yet at the same time original move. White hardly has any choice. Black can force the win by means of an ideal horizontal cutoff. }
2. Rxb6+ Kxg5 3. Ke5 Kh5 4. Rb1 g5 5. Kf5 Rf4+ 6. Ke5 Rf3 7. Rh1+ Kg6 8. Rg1
Rf4 9. Re1 Ra4 10. Rf1 g4 11. Rf4
{ A creative defensive try which I've never seen anywhere before, well worth taking notice of. }
11... Ra5+ 12. Ke4 Kg5 13. Rf1 Ra3
{ Despite White's defensive effort, an ideal horizontal cutoff is re-created one file further down. }
14. Rf8 Kh4 15. Rg8 Rf3 16. Rg7 Kh3 17. Rg8 Rf7 18. Ke3 g3 19. Ke2 Kh2 20. Rh8+
Kg1 21. Rg8 g2 22. Ra8 Rh7 23. Kf3 Kh1 { 0-1.  See Ending 62. } *

