{ Choose between 67... Ra2+, 67... Kd5 and 67... Rb1. } 1... Ra2+
{ The only move to prevent Vancura's Defence. Vancura's defensive system is clear-cut once it is established, but if getting there is impossible, as is the case here, the defender is in trouble.   67...Kd5 ?  68.Rg3 !  is Vancura's Defence.   67...Rb1 ?  prevents Vancura's Defence for now, but after  68.Ra4 !  going back with  Ra1  is no longer an option, since White improves the position of his rook with  Nor is   68...Rb3  any good, as the white king can come closer to the queenside beginning with  69.Kg2  Kd5  70.Kf2  69.Rb4  and the manoeuvre from the game no longer wins, e.g.  Ra2+  70.Kg3 !  Kd5  71.Rb3 !  and White again establishes Vancura's Defence. }
2. Kh3
{ 68.Kg3  places the Black king one square closer to the queenside, in such a way that ...Rb2 would now not be winning. The king, however, obstructs the way for the rook to the third rank. There might follow  Kd5  69.Rf4  Rb2  70.Ra4  a2  and now the Black king is too late, as in the game. }
2... Rb2 3. Ra4 a2 4. Kg3 Kd5 5. Kf3 Kc5 6. Ke3 Kb5 7. Ra8 Kc4
{ Smyslov resigned here. There might have followed   73...Kc4  74.Ra7  Kc3  75.Ra8  Kc2  76.Ra7  Kb1  -+   See Ending 66. }
*

