{ Black's pieces are miles away. Can he still draw the game ? } 1... Re6+
{ It doesn't matter that the Black king is off-side. All the rook needs to do is apply Vancura's Defence, which is perfectly viable against a pawn on the fifth rank. }
2. Kb5 Re5+
{ Black should keep giving checks until the king abandons the pawn. } 3. Kb6
Re6+ 4. Kc5 Re5+ 5. Kd6
{ Once the king is away from the pawn, the pawn itself must become the target of attack, while keeping the option open of giving lateral checks, should they be required. }
5... Rf5 6. a6 Rf6+ 7. Ke5 Rf5+ 8. Ke4 Rf6
{ Now the rook must attack the pawn from the sixth rank. } 9. Ra8 Kg7 10. Kd4
Rc6 11. Ke5 Rb6 12. Kd5 Rf6 13. Ra7+ Kg6 14. Kd4 Rc6 15. Ra8 Kg7 16. Ra7+ Kg6
17. Ke5 Rb6 18. Kd5 Rf6 19. Ke4 Rb6 20. Ke5 Rc6 21. Rd7 Rxa6 22. Rd6+ Rxd6 23.
Kxd6 { Draw.  See Ending 66. } *

