{ Is there any known defensive system available to Black ? } 1... Ke8
{ In this seemingly simple position, we are about to witness a great struggle revolving around two elementary defensive methods: Philidor's and long-side defence. Eventually Black succeeds. Given that the Black rook is badly placed on the short side, this move, aiming for Philidor's Defence, is Black's only choice. Let's see some alternatives:   89...Re8+ ?  90.Kd6  +-   89...Rh1 ?  90.Rg8+  Kc7  91.Kf7  White's king on the long side deprives Black of a viable defence. }
2. Kd6
{ Threatening 91. e6, but giving the Black rook some respite.   90.Rg1  Rh6+ !  Philidor. }
2... Rh1 3. Rg7 Ra1
{ The rook aims to give checks on the third rank from the long side.   91...Rh6+ ?  would be wrong on account of  92.e6  +- }
4. Re7+ Kf8
{ 92...Kd8  Was easier, as it doesn't allow the offer of a rook trade on the sixth rank. }
5. Rd7 Ra6+ 6. Kd5 Ke8
{ The most accurate, finally reaching the basic position of Philidor's Defence. }
7. Rd6 Ra1 { Now trading rooks is impossible. } 8. Ke6 Rh1
{ Preparing to go back to his third rank via the other side. } 9. Rd2 Rh6+ 10.
Kd5 Ra6 11. Rb2 Ra7 12. Rb6 Ke7 13. Re6+ Kd7 14. Rh6 Ra5+ 15. Ke4 Ra1
{ Draw.  See Ending 52. } *

