Kf3 7. Rf8 Ra1+ 8. Kd2 Rf1
{ Black threatens to move the pawn forward. The only way to prevent this is for White to give lateral checks from the long side, but unfortunately for him, his own king is in the way. }
9. Rf7 Kg2 10. Rg7+ Kf2 11. Rh7 f3 12. Rh2+ Kg3 13. Rh8 Ra1 14. Rg8+ Kf2 15.
