{ How many errors can you spot in the following sequence of moves: 51. Kd5 Kg5 52. Rc1 Ra6 53. Rg1 Kf6 54. Kd4 Ra3 55. Rf1 ? Here, we are about to witness some mutual lack of understanding about cutting off an enemy king: }
1. Kd3
{ would have prevented the horizontal cutoff.   51.Kd5 ?  This allows an ideal horizontal cutoff;  Kg5 ?  Black fails to seize his chance:   51...Rg4 !  52.Rc1  Ra6  53.Rg1+  Kf6  54.Kd4  Ra3  With great effort, Black has achieved an imperfect horizontal cutoff, but White's rook is correctly placed on the g-file, so the result should be a draw.  55.Rf1 ?  White shows he doesn't know the defensive technique   55.Rg2 !  55...Kg5 !  -+  56.Rg1+  Kf4  57.Rf1+  Kg4  58.Ke5  Re3+  59.Kd4  f4  60.Rg1+  Kf3  61.Rh1  Re8  62.Rf1+  Kg3  63.Kd3  f3  64.Ra1  Kh2  65.Ra7  f2  66.Rh7+  Kg2  67.Rg7+  Kf1  68.Kd2  Rd8+  69.Kc2  Rd5  0-1.  or   51.Kd4 !   See Ending 62. }
