{ What is White's only move to defend this position ? } 1. Re8
{ Against two doubled central pawns, the best option is Kling & Horwitz's defence. Therefore, the rook must be behind the pawns to capture one at the opportune moment.   90.Kg2 ?  This move would be good enough against one extra pawn, but not against two.  Rf3  91.Ra8  Intending a long-side defence, but it doesn't work against two pawns.  Rf2+ !  92.Kg1  Rd2  93.Ra3+  Ke2  94.Ra5  White has no time to take one pawn and bring the rook back to the long side.  e3  95.Kg2  Capturing the pawn with   95.Rxe5  leads to a theoretically lost ending, as the rook lacks enough checking distance:  Kf3  96.Rf5+  Ke4  97.Rf8  Rd1+  98.Kg2  e2  -+  95...Kd3+  96.Kg3  Ke4  97.Ra1  Rd4  98.Ra3  Rb4  99.Rc3  Rb1  100.Rc2  Kd3  101.Ra2  e2  102.Ra3+  Ke4  0-1. }
1... Rh1+ 2. Kg2 Re1 3. Rxe5
{ Transposing to Kling & Horwitz's defence with one pawn.  See Ending 69. } *

