{ Should White have traded rooks ? } 1. Rxf2+
{ Prematurely exchanging pieces is one of the most common errors in chess, and usually denotes an impatient character. By keeping rooks on the board   for example with  87.Ra3  White would have had to suffer a little longer, but the draw should never be in danger. If White trades rooks, he ends up in a lost pawn endgame because of an in-between check. }
1... Kxf2 2. h5 f5+
{ White missed either this move or Black's 90th. If   88...gxh5+ ?  89.Kxh5  and the f-pawn also drops. Probably, this is what White had calculated. }
3. Kf4 gxh5 4. Kxf5 Kg3 { 0-1. The h-pawn will become a queen.  See Ending 5. }
*

