[Black "Noel Studer vs. Radoslaw Wojtaszek"]
[Result "*"]
[FEN "8/4p3/8/5k2/7K/4P3/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[SetUp "1"]

{ Can White save the game ? } 1. Kg3
{ White can save the game by first defending his pawn, only to part with it later on, under the right circumstances. }
1... Ke4 2. Kf2 Kd3 3. Kf3 e5
{ White is now at a critical juncture, and has to decide what the best way is to part with his pawn. If he lets the pawn be captured on the e3-square, then the Black king would automatically be on a key square, thus ensuring promotion of the pawn within a few moves. For this reason, the correct option is: }
4. e4 Kd4 5. Kf2 Kxe4 6. Ke2 { Draw.  See Ending 80. } *

