{ It's White to move in this common endgame. Is it a draw ? } 1. Rxf7+
{ This endgame is usually won by exchanging on the f7-square, as long as the attacker keeps at least one of his pawns alive. There was no reason to postpone the sacrifice:   45.Kd6 ?  hxg5  46.hxg5  Rf5 ?  Black placidly returns the favour. Attacking the g5-pawn is good, but keeping the f7-square defended isn't. The correct move was   46...Rg1 !  47.Rxf7+  Kh8  and Black achieves the endgame rook and bishop vs. rook, which is a draw because the g5-pawn drops.  47.Rxf7+ !  This liquidation leads finally to a familiar winning endgame.  Rxf7  48.Bxf7  Kxf7  49.Kd7  Kf8  50.Ke6  Ke8  51.Kf6  Kf8  52.Kxg6  Kg8  53.Kf6  Kf8  54.g6  Kg8  55.g7  1-0. }
1... Rxf7 2. Bxf7 Kxf7 3. Kd6 hxg5 4. hxg5
{ immediately leads to a winning endgame, as seen in several exercises.  See Ending 79. }
