{ Is 65. Rxf3 enough for a draw ? } 1. Rxf3
{ Several drawing moves are available, but this is the easiest. } 1... Rg1+
{ An irrational fear for this move might lead a player to decide against playing the safe 65. Rxf3, but the pawn endgame is a draw. }
2. Kxg1 Kxf3 3. Kf1
{ The white position is unassailable. Black can't win even if his pawn were on f7, since White would always be able to play a well-timed f2-f4. Black, however, would be able to win if there were other pawns, for example a fixed pair of pawns on the b-file. }
3... f5 4. Ke1 Kg2
{ 68...f4  69.Kf1  isn't winning either. Now is the right time to give up the pawn. }
