{ What can White hope for ? } 1. fxg5
{ Black has just played ...g6-g5, and by doing so he has given White the option to create a decisive outside passed pawn. This exchange, coupled with a subsequent king transfer to g4, enables White to create an outside passed pawn. There is little Black can do. }
1... hxg5 2. Kf3 Kg6 3. Kg4 f5+
{ If Black waits with the king, White will play g2-g3 and h2-h4. } 4. exf6 Kxf6
5. g3 a5 6. a4 e5 7. h4 gxh4 8. gxh4
{ White is now the proud owner of an outside passed pawn. The next step is to divert Black's king by giving it up, allowing his own king to gobble up all the enemy pawns. }
8... Kg6 9. b3 b6 10. h5+ Kf6 11. h6 Kg6 12. h7 Kxh7 13. Kf5
{ Black resigned.  See Ending 90. } *

