{ Can Black win the game ? } 1... Rxf3+
{ This position may look rather confusing, but Black can once again force an endgame with a blocked pawn by a couple of accurate checks, an idea we've seen before.  The rook sacrifice ensures the creation of a dangerous pawn duo which forces White to give back his rook but in worse conditions. Not good enough to win is   51...gxf3  52.gxf3  h3  53.Rh2  Rxf3+  54.Ke4 =  or   51...h3  52.gxh3  Rxh3  53.Ke4 = }
2. gxf3 g3
{ The threat of the g3/h4-pawn duo turning into an unstoppable force paralyses the rook, so the king must intervene. }
3. Ke2 h3 4. Kf1 gxf2
{ Perfect timing. Black forces through simplification, and now proceeds to wrest control over the key squares away from the opponent. }
5. Kxf2 Kxb4 6. Kg1 Kc3 7. Kh2 Kd3 8. Kxh3 Ke2 9. Kg2 Ke3 10. Kf1 Kxf3 11. Ke1
Kg2 12. Ke2 f3+ { 0-1.  See Ending 79. } *

