{ Choose between 56. Ke6 and 56. Kd7. } 1. Ke6
{ Our celebrated forebears were fully aware of how effective this kind of blocked pawn duo is in helping to tear down a fortress. They also knew how to play accurately.   56.Kd6  also wins, with the same idea.  By contrast,   56.Kd7 ?  is inadequate:  56...fxg5  57.Re7+  Kf6 !!  Avoiding a transition into a lost pawn endgame, to get into a drawn rook endgame instead.  58.Rxh7  gxh4  59.Rxh4  g5  60.Rh8  Ke5 ! = }
1... fxg5 2. Re7+ Kh6 3. Rxh7+ Kxh7 4. hxg5 { The rest is easy. } 4... Kg7 5.
