{ Can White win the game ? } 1. Kd4
{ The point is to execute a dual-purpose king manoeuvre: capture the f7-pawn while shouldering off  ('bodychecking')  the enemy king. Of course, accurate calculation is required.   61.Ke5 ?  White can't win by a direct race. He must use the mechanism of the bodycheck to force Black to either worsen his king position or move the pawn.  Kc5 !  62.f3  Kc6  63.f4   63.Kf6  Kd5 !  64.Kxf7  Ke5 =  63...Kd7  64.Kf6  Ke8  65.Kg7  f5 !  66.Kf6  Draw. }
1... Kb5
{ if the king moves up, White will keep the opposition while getting closer to the f7-pawn; if the king moves down,   61...Kb3  the pawn moves up:  62.f4  Kc2  63.f5  Kd2  64.f6  Ke2  65.Kd5  +-   61...f6  62.f4  Kb5  63.Kd5  Kb4  64.Ke6  +- }
2. Kd5 Kb6 3. Kd6 { See Ending 80. } *

