{ Can Black get a fortress? } 1... Be6
{ In blitz games, even elite players sometimes mess up simple endgames.   74...Bg4 ??  Black can set up a fortress, but he is going to have to work for it. Before anything else, the bishop must take the a2-g8 diagonal.  75.Ke5 !  Now the bishop can't get back onto the right diagonal.  Bf3  76.Ra7+  Kf8  77.Rc7   77.f7 !  is much faster:  Kg7  78.Ke6  Bh5  79.Rc7  (zugzwang)  Bg6  80.f8=Q+  Kxf8  81.Kf6  +-  77...Bg4  78.Kd5  Bf3+  79.Ke5  Bg4  80.Rc4  Bf3  81.Ke6  Bb7  82.f7  Ba6  83.Rh4  Kg7  84.Rg4+  1-0.   74...Bc8  is another possibility, because it attacks the rook and so the bishop could go to e6 on the next turn. }
2. Ke5 Bb3 { See Ending 97. } *

