{ Choose between 106... Ra8 and 106... Bc4. } 1... Ra8+
{ Black can force the Philidor position. At this exact moment, however, Black in practice often deviates from the right plan, and often sees his winning chances vanish into thin air after the opponent finds the second-rank defence.   106...Bc4 ?  The move in the game might seem winning, but is adequately countered by:  107.Rb5+ !  This stalemate resource throws a spanner in the works, kicking away Black's king. White now correctly engineers the second-rank defence.  Kd4  108.Rb6  Rh5+  109.Kb4  Rh2  110.Rd6+  Bd5  111.Rb6  Rc2  112.Ka5  Bc4  113.Kb4  Rc1  114.Rd6+  Bd5  115.Rb6  Bc6  116.Ka5  Bd7  117.Rb4+  Kd5  118.Kb6  Rc6+  119.Kb7  Re6  120.Rb1  Bc6+  121.Kb6  Be8+  122.Kc7  Ba4  123.Ra1  Bb5  124.Rd1+  Draw. }
2. Ra6 Rb8 { starts the correct execution of Philidor's plan: } 3. Rh6 Rb3 4.
Rh4 Bf3 5. Rf4 Bc6 6. Rf5+ Bd5 7. Rf4 Rb5+ 8. Ka4 Rb7 9. Ka3 Rb3+ 10. Ka4 Re3
