{ White to move. Does Black have a fortress ? } 1. Qb3+
{ would prevent Black's king from stepping inside the fortress, and White would be winning, e. g.   109.Qa7+ ?  Black's fortress has one major flaw: the king isn't inside. Fortunately for him, White allows it in.  Kg8 !  From now on, Black has a rock-solid fortress, and the defence is straightforward, despite White's understandable attempt to get anywhere.  110.Qb8+  Kh7  111.Kg5  Nf7+  112.Kh5  Ne5  113.Qc8  Bh8  114.Kg5  Bg7  115.Qe8  Bh6+  116.Kf5  Bg7  117.Qh5+  Kg8  118.Ke6  Bh8  119.Ke7  Bg7  120.Qh1  Ng6+  121.Ke8  Ne5  122.Qh3  Bh8  123.Qh2  Bg7  124.Qh3  Bh8  125.Qe6+  Kh7  126.Qh3+  Kg8  127.Qh6  Bg7  128.Qxg7+  Draw. }
1... Kf8 2. Qd5
{ with zugzwang - the obligation to move creates disarray in Black's camp: }
