{ Has White destroyed the Black fortress ? } 1... Kg7
{ was the right move. It is more important to keep the enemy king out than to unpin. The g6-pawn will be lost in any case, and at least this move lures the white pawn closer, enabling Black to later capture it to force a drawn rook vs. bishop ending:  From the fortress rook and two pawns vs. bishop and two pawns in the corner, it is possible to get to this position almost by force. The fortress isn't falling apart yet, but Black faces a crucial decision.   91...Kh7 ?  92.Kf7 !  Kh6  93.Rxg6+  Kh5  Now Black won't be able to capture the white pawn.  94.Rg2   94.Rg4  looks like an easier win.  94...Bc3  95.Rh2  Be5  96.Rh1  Bg3  97.Kf6  Bc7  98.Kf5  Bg3  99.Rd1  Bh2  100.Rd2  Bg1  101.Kf4  1-0. }
