{ Can Black save the game ? } 1... Rxc7
{ Black can save the game, provided he immediately sacrifices the exchange. By doing so, he will have enough time to use his king, first to force the a5-pawn to move forward, and, after that, to hide in the corner. }
2. Nxc7 Kxc7 3. Kf3 Kd6
{ Objectively, with this move most of the hard work has been done. Now White will be forced to move the pawn up to the a6-square. }
4. Ke4
{ 60.a6  would lead to an immediate fortress. The game move forces Black to hang in tough. }
4... Kc5 5. Be2 Kb4
{ By the skin of his teeth ! Black is just in time to attack the pawn and to get back. That said, playing ...a7-a6 would also be good enough, since this would force the capture of the pawn. }
6. a6 Kc5 7. Ke5 Kc6 { Draw. } *

