{ Three moves draw. Which ones ? } 1. a8=Q+
{ This was a bit of a trick question: the three moves that draw are:   55.a8=R+  or   55.a8=B  The reason is that the White king needs access to the c2-square to capture the c-pawn.   55.a8=N ?  loses to  (Kb7 ! -+)  other moves lose the pawn without diverting the Black bishop. }
1... Bxa8 2. Kc2 Bc6 3. Kxc3 Bb5
{ Before hiding in the corner, White's king must force the Black h-pawn forward. Without this, Black would win by means of a simple procedure: 1 Stalemate White's king on the h1-square and force him to play h2-h3; 2 Capture that pawn; and 3 Promote. }
4. Kd4 f1=Q 5. Bxf1 Bxf1 6. Ke3 Kb5 7. Kf4 h3 8. Ke3 Kc4 9. Kf2 Bg2 { Draw. } *

