{ Choose between 59. Kd4 and 59. Kf4. } 1. Kd4
{ prevents Black from executing his plan:   59.Kf4 ?  Black's king faces a laborious task: not only must it first create the fortress - by forcing the b5-pawn up to the b6-square - it also needs to go back all the way and hide inside it. Getting all of this done is obviously time-consuming. White, however, wastes all his advantage with a greedy move.  h3  60.Kxg3  hxg2  61.Kxg2  Kd5  62.Kg3  Kc5  Black executes the first stage on the plan.  63.b6  Kc6  64.Kxg4  Kd7  65.Kf4  Kc8  Mission accomplished: this is now an impenetrable fortress.  66.Ke4  Kd7  67.Kd5  Kc8  68.Bh2  Kd7  69.Be5  Kc8  70.Kd6  Kb8  71.Kd7+  Ka8  72.Bb8  Kxb8  73.Kd8  Ka8  74.Kc8  Draw.   59.Ke4 !  also wins, based on the same motif. }
1... h3 2. Bxg3 hxg2 3. Bf2 { 61.Bh2  Kf5  62.Kd3  is a more complicated win }
3... Kf5 4. Be3 g3 5. Kd5 Kg4 6. Ke4 Kh5 7. Kf4 Kh4 8. Bg1 Kh5 9. Kxg3 Kg5 10.
Kxg2 Kf4 11. Kf2 Ke4 12. Ke2 Kd5 13. Kd3
{ and Black's king can't attack the White pawn. } *

