{ Choose between 57... Bc4 and 57... Bg8. } 1... Bg8
{ moves the bishop back in anticipation of the pawn coming to the h7-square:   57...Bc4 ?  White would love to get the fortress from the previous exercise. To do so, he must entice Black to play ...b4-b3. Black, therefore, must be wary of this idea. He has two good options, but this is not one of them.  58.Kf5  Kh6  59.Ke4  Now it's clear that White will be able to carry his plan through.  b3  Black acquiesces. The fortress stands erect and all White has to do now is hide the king inside.  60.Ke3  Kh5  61.Kd2  Kxh4  62.Kc1  Bd3  63.Kd2  Bc2  64.Kc3  Kg3  65.Kd2  Kf3  66.Kc1  Ke3  Draw.  The second correct option is based on the same idea:   57...Kf7 !  58.h5  Ke7  59.h6  Bg8  60.Kf5  Kd6  and Black's king reaches the queenside in time. }
2. Kf5 Kf7 3. Ke5 Ke7 4. h5
{ 60.Kd4  Kd6  61.h5  Kc6  62.h6  and White lacks one tempo:  (Kb5 ! -+) } 4...
Kd7 5. h6 Kc6 6. h7 Bxh7 7. Kd4 Kb5 *

